28:["$","p","p-7",{"children":["If training loss falls while validation loss rises, the model may be fitting details peculiar to the training set. This is ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"overfitting"}],". It can also signal a split or distribution problem, so inspect examples before changing architecture. First responses include more representative data, a simpler model, regularization, or stopping training earlier. A large model is not automatically the best baseline."]}]
29:["$","p","p-8",{"children":"For ticket routing, begin with a keyword rule, then a simple text classifier. Track both against the same held-out tickets. A neural model is worth considering only when the simpler candidates miss a valuable pattern and the added operating cost is justified."}]
